-- title:
--   Integrality of Ogg's unit and p¹²u⁻¹ over ℤ[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Inside the field $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $u = \mathtt{modularUnitSeries}\,p$ be the quotient $\Delta \cdot (\Delta^{(p)})^{-1}$, where $\Delta$ is the series $q$ times the power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ` and $\Delta^{(p)}$ is its substitution $q \mapsto q^{p}$ under `qExpand`, and let $F = \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,p$ be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the expansions $j(q^{d})$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid p$, i.e. by $j(q)$ and $j(q^{p})$. Assume $u \in F$, and let $j = \mathtt{IgusaScheme.jFull}\,p$ denote the element $j(q)$ of $F$. The subalgebra $\mathtt{AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin}\ \mathbb{Z}\ F\ j$ consists of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by $j$, that is, the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}[j]$ in $F$. The assertion is the conjunction: the element $u$ of $F$ lies in this subalgebra, and so does $p^{12} u^{-1}$, the product of the image of $p^{12}$ in $F$ with the inverse of $u$ in $F$. No prime is inverted: the base ring is $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This records the integrality properties of Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{p})$ on the finite ($j$-integral) chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(p)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, the second half expressing that the Fricke image $p^{12}/u$ of the unit is regular there as well. It feeds the lemmas on the Deligne–Rapoport model package ([`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.modularUnitSeries_mem_chartAlgFin_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.modularUnitSeries_mem_chartAlgFin_mul) and the statements on locally split pools and on stalks at crossing points).
